# === Inference and results: a p-value carries its full frame =============== #

ex:ecPValueWellFramed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/pvalue-well-framed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:PValue carrying its whole frame — a math:testStatistic, a math:nullHypothesis, a parameterized math:nullDistribution (a math:SamplingDistribution), and a math:alternativeSidedness that IS one of the six lawful math:Sidedness values (math:twoSidedAlternative) — with its magnitude a framed math:ProbabilityValue (exact 3/100 in [0, 1]). Every arm of math:IllFramedPValueShape is satisfied so its SPARQL stays silent, the lawful sidedness satisfies math:AlternativeSidednessValueShape's sh:in, the framed value satisfies math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape / math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape / math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape / math:RationalValueShape, and the null distribution satisfies the P6a/P6b/P7 gates, so validation emits no findings." .

ex:ecPValueMissingSidednessBad a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/pvalue-missing-sidedness.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is the SAME math:PValue fully framed — a math:testStatistic, a math:nullHypothesis, a parameterized math:nullDistribution, and a framed math:ProbabilityValue magnitude — EXCEPT it omits BOTH math:tailDefinition AND math:alternativeSidedness, so the tail-or-sidedness arm of math:IllFramedPValueShape fires. math:AlternativeSidednessValueShape's sh:in is satisfied vacuously (no math:alternativeSidedness value to check), the framed value still satisfies the probability-value shapes, and the null distribution keeps the distribution gates silent, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:IllFramedPValue)." .

ex:ecPValueHypothesisTestFramed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/pvalue-hypothesis-test-framed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:PValue whose test arm is satisfied via the math:HypothesisTest whose math:pValue it is (the statistic lives on the test, not the p-value) rather than a direct math:testStatistic; every arm of math:IllFramedPValueShape is satisfied so its SPARQL stays silent, the lawful sidedness (math:twoSidedAlternative) satisfies math:AlternativeSidednessValueShape's sh:in, the framed value satisfies math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape / math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape / math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape / math:RationalValueShape, and the null distribution satisfies the P6a/P6b/P7 gates; it exercises the HypothesisTest path of the shape's test arm, so validation emits no findings." .

# === The signature lang: -> logic: -> math: p-value round-trip ============== #

ex:ecPValueTriSlice a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/pvalue-tri-slice.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The signature round-trip as one grounded chain: the sentence 'the p-value was 0.03' as a lang:SurfaceForm realizing an analyzed lang:ComposedForm, a lang:Denotation (lang:denotesLogicFormula) whose lang:denotationTarget is a logic:Formula, and that formula's first argument (logic:termIri) being the math:PValue. The math:PValue carries its whole frame — a math:testStatistic, a math:nullHypothesis, a parameterized math:nullDistribution (a math:SamplingDistribution), and a math:alternativeSidedness that IS one of the six lawful math:Sidedness values (math:twoSidedAlternative) — with its magnitude a framed math:ProbabilityValue (exact 3/100 in [0, 1]). Every arm of math:IllFramedPValueShape is satisfied so its SPARQL stays silent, the lawful sidedness satisfies math:AlternativeSidednessValueShape's sh:in, the framed value satisfies math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape / math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape / math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape / math:RationalValueShape, and the null distribution satisfies the P6a/P6b/P7 gates, so validation emits no findings." .

ex:ecPValueTriSliceIllframedBad a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/pvalue-tri-slice-illframed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is the SAME lang: -> logic: -> math: round-trip fully grounded — a lang:SurfaceForm realizing a lang:ComposedForm, a lang:Denotation targeting a logic:Formula, and that formula predicating over the math:PValue — EXCEPT the p-value omits BOTH math:tailDefinition AND math:alternativeSidedness, so the tail-or-sidedness arm of math:IllFramedPValueShape fires. math:AlternativeSidednessValueShape's sh:in is satisfied vacuously (no math:alternativeSidedness value to check), the framed value still satisfies the probability-value shapes, and the null distribution keeps the distribution gates silent, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:IllFramedPValue)." .

# === Inference and results: a confidence interval carries its bounds and level (Rule I4) === #

ex:ecConfidenceIntervalComplete a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/confidence-interval-complete.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:ConfidenceInterval naming its two bounds through math:hasIntervalBound (satisfying sh:minCount 2) and its coverage through math:confidenceLevel — a framed math:ProbabilityValue, exact 95/100 in [0, 1] — satisfies math:IncompleteConfidenceIntervalShape; being no math:CredibleInterval it satisfies math:IntervalKindConflationShape's sh:not, and its framed rational level satisfies the probability-value shapes, so validation emits no findings." .

ex:ecConfidenceIntervalIncomplete a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/confidence-interval-incomplete.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a math:ConfidenceInterval carrying its two math:hasIntervalBound endpoints but omitting math:confidenceLevel (sh:minCount 1 on math:IncompleteConfidenceIntervalShape); its two bounds keep the bound arm satisfied and it is not a math:CredibleInterval so math:IntervalKindConflationShape stays satisfied, so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval)." .

# === Inference and results: a credible interval carries its posterior and mass (Rule I5) === #

