ex:ecIntervalKindConflation a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/interval-kind-conflation.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.NotConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is ONE node typed BOTH math:ConfidenceInterval and math:CredibleInterval, tripping the sh:not [ sh:class math:CredibleInterval ] of math:IntervalKindConflationShape. It is COMPLETE for both kinds — its two math:hasIntervalBound endpoints and framed math:confidenceLevel satisfy math:IncompleteConfidenceIntervalShape, and its math:hasPosterior and framed math:credibleMass satisfy math:IncompleteCredibleIntervalShape — so ONLY the sh:not fires: validation MUST emit shacl.NotConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:IntervalKindConflation)." .

