# === Flagship acceptance manifest: the failure-range shape bites ============= #
#
# The shared cardinality wiring (an example, competency, producer, counter-example, and
# enforcing class, each exactly once) is now the shared gmeow:FlagshipScenarioShape's job
# (shapes/gmeow-shapes.ttl), gated positively over examples/flagship-acceptance.ttl by
# `make validate` and by the native flagship cross-check (a missing required link drops the
# scenario from the coverage set). This slice's thin math:FlagshipScenarioShape carries
# ONLY the failure-range sh:sparql, so the per-slice conformance cells exercise exactly
# that: a well-formed scenario conforms, and one whose enforcing class is not a
# math:MathConformanceFailure subclass raises shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent.

ex:ecFlagshipCanonical a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/flagship-scenario-canonical.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A gmeow:FlagshipScenario binding all artifacts (gmeow:demonstratedByExample, gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency, gmeow:demonstratedByProducer, gmeow:guardedByCounterExample) and naming an enforcing failure class that IS a math:MathConformanceFailure subclass (math:WrongE8WeylOrder) passes the slice's thin math:FlagshipScenarioShape failure-range sh:sparql, and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecFlagshipNonFailureClass a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/flagship-scenario-nonfailure-class.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a gmeow:FlagshipScenario whose gmeow:enforcesFailureClass names math:Set — a real class that is NOT a math:MathConformanceFailure subclass (the failure-range sh:sparql of the slice's thin math:FlagshipScenarioShape). That constraint fires, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (math:UnwiredFlagshipScenario) — the enforcing failure class is checked by value." .

# =========================================================================== #
# Probability-layer gates (Rules P1–P11 of shapes.ttl) — each SHACL/SHACL-SPARQL
# gate gets one conforming fixture and one counter-example isolating exactly one
# violation. See slices/grounding/math/design/MATHEMATICS-PROBABILITY.md.
# =========================================================================== #

# === Rule P1: a probability value's magnitude lies in the closed unit interval [0,1] === #

ex:ecProbabilityValueInUnit a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/probability-value-in-unit.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A framed math:ProbabilityValue carrying its exact magnitude 0.72 as a math:RationalValue 18/25 (exact-rational discipline, AC#6) satisfies math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape, math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape, math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape, math:ConfidenceAsProbabilityConstraint and math:RationalValueShape, validating with no findings." .

ex:ecProbabilityValueAboveUnitBad a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/probability-value-above-unit.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MaxInclusiveConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a framed math:ProbabilityValue whose gmeow:quantityValue (1.5) exceeds the closed unit interval's sh:maxInclusive 1 on math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape, so validation MUST emit shacl.MaxInclusiveConstraintComponent and NO other finding — the frame keeps math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape satisfied (math:ProbabilityOutOfBounds)." .

# === Rule P2: a probability value is never also an odds or log-odds value === #

ex:ecOddsValueDistinct a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/odds-value-distinct.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:OddsValue that is NOT typed math:ProbabilityValue, recovering its probability through a declared math:ProbabilityScaleTransform, faces none of the probability-value gates and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecProbabilityScaleConflationBad a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/probability-scale-conflation.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.NotConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a node typed BOTH math:ProbabilityValue and math:OddsValue, tripping the sh:not [ sh:class math:OddsValue ] of math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape, so validation MUST emit shacl.NotConstraintComponent and NO other finding — the frame keeps math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape satisfied (math:ProbabilityScaleConflation)." .

# === Rule P3: a probability value names its reference frame or its probability model === #

ex:ecProbabilityValueFramed a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/probability-value-framed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:ProbabilityValue naming its gmeow:hasReferenceFrame, carrying its exact magnitude 1/2 as a math:RationalValue (AC#6), satisfies the sh:or of math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecProbabilityValueUnframedBad a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/probability-value-unframed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.OrConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a math:ProbabilityValue naming NEITHER gmeow:hasReferenceFrame NOR logic:probabilityModel, so the sh:or of math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape fails; validation MUST emit shacl.OrConstraintComponent and NO other finding — its in-range 0.5 keeps math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape satisfied (math:UnframedProbabilityValue)." .

# === Rule P4: a probability space names all three Kolmogorov-triple components === #

ex:ecProbabilitySpaceComplete a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/probability-space-complete.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:ProbabilitySpace naming a symbolic math:SymbolicSampleSpace, a math:BorelSigmaAlgebra, and a total-mass-one math:ProbabilityMeasure satisfies math:ProbabilitySpaceCompleteShape (and the inherited measure shapes) and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecProbabilitySpaceIncompleteBad a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/probability-space-incomplete.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a math:ProbabilitySpace naming its sample space and σ-algebra but omitting its math:probabilityMeasure (sh:minCount 1 on math:ProbabilitySpaceCompleteShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:IncompleteProbabilitySpace)." .

# === Rule P5: a random variable declares its domain, codomain, and a context === #

ex:ecRandomVariableScoped a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/random-variable-scoped.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:RandomVariable declaring math:randomVariableDomain, math:randomVariableCodomain, and a math:hasDistribution context (to a family-named distribution) satisfies math:RandomVariableScopedShape and validates with no findings." .

ex:ecRandomVariableUnscopedBad a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/random-variable-unscoped.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a math:RandomVariable with a domain and a distribution context but no math:randomVariableCodomain (sh:minCount 1 on math:RandomVariableScopedShape), so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding — its family-named distribution keeps math:DistributionFamilyShape satisfied (math:UnscopedRandomVariable)." .

# === Rule P6a: a distribution names its family (MinCount) === #

ex:ecDistributionParameterized a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/distribution-parameterized.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:Distribution naming its math:distributionFamily and its math:distributionParameterization, supplying each required role exactly once, satisfies math:DistributionFamilyShape, math:DistributionParameterizationShape, and math:ParameterRoleCardinalityConstraint, validating with no findings." .

ex:ecDistributionMissingFamilyBad a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/distribution-missing-family.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a bare math:Distribution naming no math:distributionFamily (sh:minCount 1 on math:DistributionFamilyShape); supplying no parameters keeps the parametric SPARQL gates silent, so validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:MissingDistributionParameterization)." .

# === Rule P6b: a parameter-supplying distribution names its parameterization (SPARQL) === #

ex:ecDistributionMissingParameterizationBad a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/distribution-missing-parameterization.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a parametric math:Distribution (it supplies a math:hasDistributionParameter) that names no math:distributionParameterization, tripping the SHACL-SPARQL of math:DistributionParameterizationShape; its named math:distributionFamily keeps math:DistributionFamilyShape satisfied, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:MissingDistributionParameterization)." .

# === Rule P7: each required parameter role is supplied exactly once (SPARQL) === #

ex:ecDistributionRoleExact a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/distribution-role-exact.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "A math:Distribution whose parameterization requires one rate role, supplied by exactly one math:DistributionParameter, keeps math:ParameterRoleCardinalityConstraint silent (and satisfies P6a/P6b), validating with no findings." .

ex:ecDistributionRoleCardinalityBad a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/distribution-role-cardinality.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example is a math:Distribution whose parameterization requires one rate role but which supplies it TWICE, so the aggregate per-role count (2 ≠ 1) trips the SHACL-SPARQL of math:ParameterRoleCardinalityConstraint; its named family and parameterization keep P6a/P6b satisfied, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:DistributionParameterRoleCardinality)." .

